new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/FUNCTIONAL_CHECK.md
@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+# Reference API functional checks
+
+This patch adds a standalone harness; it does not change cryptographic sources
+or load any structural recovery code. Run it from a copy of the supplied
+Reference_Implementation directory containing Facto-DSA-128, -256 and -512:
+
+```sh
+patch --dry-run -p1 < /absolute/path/reference-functional-check.patch
+patch -p1 < /absolute/path/reference-functional-check.patch
+python3 check_functional.py --output /absolute/path/fresh-test-results
+```
+
+Alternatively, without applying the patch, run the provided script with
+`--source /absolute/path/Reference_Implementation` and an output directory.
+Requirements: Python 3 and a C99 compiler (`cc`, or use `--cc clang`). No Python
+packages or network access are needed. Compiled binaries use temporary paths.
+
+For each of the three parameter sets the harness calls the supplied DRNG,
+sig_keygen, sig_sign and sig_verify with message lengths 0, 1 and 56 bytes.
+Each case uses a newly generated key. Checks cover returned lengths, successful
+verification, rejection of an appended message byte and rejection of a signature
+with its final byte removed. The runner also compares the parameter and length
+values with specification Table 2 and records source hashes before/after.
+
+The fixed seeds are test fixtures only, never production key material. Secret
+keys stay in process memory and are wiped before free; the harness writes no
+key, signature or seed payload. JSON output contains only metadata and return
+codes. Thus these artifacts validate ordinary API functionality, not Recovery,
+forgery, security levels, all possible keys or exact PDF conformance.
+
+Each compile has a 60-second timeout; each parameter-set executable has a
+180-second default timeout, adjustable with --timeout. A failed case or timeout
+is recorded and never automatically retried. Existing results.json is not
+overwritten. The runner continues to the other independent parameter sets.
